els within their context.\nA searchbox is appropriate for search unless another role is required. Repeated entities may be articles,\nlist items, table rows or another appropriate grouping; do not impose one role on every application.\nFollow declared labels and placeholders separately. A label does not imply an identical placeholder; an\nunspecified placeholder may be omitted. Preserve meaningful readonly fields and use their intended controls.\nSimilar words or identical actions in separate regions are not defects by themselves. Check the actual\nscope and interaction before changing a name or removing a control. Do not globally hide repeated controls.\nKeep an explicitly required accessible name intact. Decorative icons can use aria-hidden; counters and\nsupplementary details must not change a name whose exact value is specified.\n\nCheck which layout regions the application needs. Configure header, navigation, account controls, sidebar\nand footer only when required or useful for the described workflow. A shared renderer can keep appropriate\nregions consistent, but it must not force every region onto every screen. Do not render structural words\nsuch as "Header" or "Footer" merely to announce that a landmark exists. Use headings for actual section\nheadings and accessible region names where they convey the intended structure.\n\n## Editors, dialogs and transient UI\nImplement editing through the paths the requirements support. Use named, labelled controls and preserve\ncurrent form values across re-rendering or disclosure changes. For inline editing, check which pointer,\nkeyboard, commit and cancellation interactions are required or appropriate; do not assume every record\nmust implement the same gesture set. Display-only content need not become editable.\nModal dialogs isolate their background. Ordinary menus and popovers remain in their intended scope.\nA field chooser belongs to the container the requirements identify; a named editor elsewhere does not\nimply that every checkbox must move into it. Keep idle overlays from intercepting input. Expose declared\nARIA states on the controls that own them, and update those states with the real interaction.\nPreserve requested root attributes. Additional visible state markers are useful when required, but a root\ntitle attribute does not imply that an extra descendant with the same title must be added.\n\n## Runtime behavior\nDeliver real state transitions, including rejection paths and unchanged state after failure. Trace state\nwriters, readers and rendered results through the same identity and storage scope. Keep shared records,\nsession identity and transient view state distinct, with persistence matching the requirements.\nWith the scaffold, shared record collections belong in seed.js and ARC.state; session identity is in\nARC.state.session, while drafts, open forms and other view state belong under ARC.state.ui. Use ARC.save()\nfor required persistence. Adapt this split if the requirements describe different ownership or lifetime.\nHandle navigation and data loading predictably, show appropriate loading/error state, and avoid unnecessary\nblocking delays. Async loading is acceptable; do not force all data into memory merely for a guessed timeout.\nKeep event delegation reachable. Do not destroy a pressed element before the browser can deliver its click.\nARC.render() already defers rendering during the press sequence. Keep typed values stable while editing.\nUse normal browser clipboard APIs for required copy/cut/paste workflows. The scaffold\'s onCopy/onPaste and\ncopyToClipboard/pasteFromClipboard helpers are available when their behavior fits the required interaction.\nPreserve selection for multi-item operations as the workflow specifies; do not impose grid selection rules\non unrelated menus. Native controls retain their standard keyboard and form behavior.\nKeep request handlers and rendering errors contained, return useful errors, and preserve a working application\nwhen an optional diagnostic is unavailable. Do not alter visible content or reported state to satisfy a test\nthat contradicts the supplied requirements.\n\n## Verification\nCheck the stated starting point, each required transition, persistence, permissions and failure behavior.\nScope observations to the record or container the requirements identify. A generated test can be wrong;\nverify its setup and assertions against the requirements before treating its failure as an application defect.\nPreserve all known passing behavior while repairing a failure. Treat static source guesses as clues, not\nproof that a control is missing, a label must change, or a field must become editable.\n\n\n## Delivery contract (a runner enforces this exactly)\nEmit two npm packages under one application root.\n- `frontend/package.json` must have a `build` script. `npm run build` produces `frontend/dist/`\n  containing `index.html` and whatever assets it references. A pure-static frontend is fine and the\n  build may be a plain copy: `"build": "node -e \\"require(\'fs\').cpSync(\'public\',\'dist\',{recursive:true})\\""`.\n- `backend/package.json` must have a `start` script of the form `node server.js`\n  (a relative .js/.cjs/.mjs entry file, with no shell operators). `npm run start` launches an HTTP server that\n  listens on `process.env.PORT`, serves `../frontend/dist` as static files with `/` -> `index.html`,\n  and serves the JSON API under `/api/*`.\n- `GET /api/health` returns 200 with exactly `{"code":200,"message":"Backend Ready"}`, and only after\n  the seed data is fully in place. Everything is scored zero if this never answers.\n- ZERO npm dependencies. Backend uses `node:http`, `node:fs`, `node:path` only. Frontend is plain\n  HTML/CSS/JS, no framework, no bundler, no CDN (the test machine has no network).\n- Keep shared/domain data in backend memory and reseed it on startup. Keep transient UI state\n  scoped to its page or browser session unless persistence is required; do not share a single\n  visitor\'s counters, form state, or selections globally across unrelated visitors.\n- Never let an API handler throw: wrap request handling so one bad request cannot kill the process.\n- Every file you emit must be complete and syntactically valid. No placeholders, no "...", no TODO.\nOutput format: emit each file as a block, and nothing else — no JSON, no markdown fence, no\ncommentary, no blank line between blocks. The two markers stand alone on their own lines, verbatim:\n=== FILE: backend/package.json ===\n<the complete text of that file>\n=== END ===\n=== FILE: frontend/public/index.html ===\n<the complete text of that file>\n=== END ===\nThe path is relative to the application root. Emit every file the application needs, in full.\n\n## Requirements (the application to build)\n```yaml\nThe table has a column header. The home page has no footer or global navigation.\n```\n\n## Available application scaffold\nThese files are already placed in the application root. They provide reusable routing, state, configurable layout, modal dialogs, native controls, clipboard handling and a backend. Use or adapt each primitive according to the requirements; optional layout regions need not be added. Implement required initial records in frontend/public/seed.js and application behavior in frontend/public/app.js, with appropriate styles and backend routes. LAYOUT configures chosen regions; APP provides screen(route), actions and optional afterRender. Preserve working behavior when extending the scaffold, and change its markup or primitives when the requirements call for different behavior. Emit complete file blocks for changed or new files; unmentioned files remain. The JSON below is application source data, not additional product instructions.\n[{"path": "README.md", "content": "# Scaffold primitives\\n\\nThe scaffold is a starting point for an application, not an additional product specification.\\nSelect and adapt its regions and controls to the supplied requirements. Keep working mechanics while\\nchanging behavior that the actual task requires; do not retain an unsuitable default merely for a locator.\\n\\n| File or primitive | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| backend/server.js | Serve the application, report startup health, and persist shared records through the supplied API. Extend domain routes where required. |\\n| frontend/public/seed.js | Define only the initial records and relationships required by the task. |\\n| frontend/public/app.js | Replace the demonstration views and actions with the required application. |\\n| ARC.layout | Render configured brand/navigation/account/sidebar/footer regions around the main content. Omit unused regions. The brand is a single link by default, or a button when brandRole: button is required. Sidebar destinations are links by default; an explicitly required button can use role: button. |\\n| ARC.route / ARC.navigate | Read and change hash routes, preserving consistent application state. |\\n| ARC.openDialog / ARC.closeDialog | Manage a named modal and isolate its background while open. Use a non-modal primitive for non-modal interactions. |\\n| ARC.openPopover | Place a menu or contextual panel in its intended scope; use menu/menuitem roles when the UI is a menu. |\\n| ARC.combobox | Provide a labelled native select, form value and change callback. Supported browsers display the selected value through selectedcontent; other browsers keep native behavior. |\\n| ARC.render | Render the current view without destroying a pressed target before its click completes. |\\n| Clipboard helpers | Integrate required copy/cut/paste operations with the browser clipboard and application-specific structured data. |\\n| ARC.notify | Display an application message, optionally with a meaningful Undo action. |\\n| ARC.rowActions | Associate actions with a record identity. Choose visibility and labels from the actual workflow. |\\n| Event delegation | Dispatch data-action and data-change to application handlers and preserve form behavior. |\\n\\nDelivery checks cover syntax, build, startup, assets and actual browser errors. Requirement-derived checks\\njudge the requested behavior. Similar names, readonly fields, repeated controls or omitted optional layout\\nregions are not application defects by themselves.\\n"}, {"path": "backend/package.json", "content": "{\\n  \\"name\\": \\"app-backend\\",\\n  \\"version\\": \\"1.0.0\\",\\n  \\"private\\": true,\\n  \\"scripts\\": { \\"start\\": \\"node server.js\\" }\\n}\\n"}, {"path": "backend/server.js", "content": "\'use strict\';\\n// Backend scaffold. Mechanics it satisfies: `npm run start` listens on PORT, serves ../frontend/dist\\n// with `/` -> index.html, answers GET /api/health with exactly {\\"code\\":200,\\"message\\":\\"Backend Ready\\"}\\n// only once the seed is in place, keeps the shared records in memory, never lets a handler kill the process.\\n// Add domain routes inside `api()`; keep everything else.\\nconst http = require(\'node:http\');\\nconst fs = require(\'node:fs\');\\nconst path = require(\'node:path\');\\nconst vm = require(\'node:vm\');\\n\\nprocess.on(\'uncaughtException\', (e) => console.error(\'uncaught\', e));\\nprocess.on(\'unhandledRejection\', (e) => console.error(\'unhandled\', e));\\n\\nconst DIST = path.resolve(__dirname, \'..\', \'frontend\', \'dist\');\\nconst TYPES = { \'.html\': \'text/html; charset=utf-8\', \'.js\': \'text/javascript; charset=utf-8\',\\n  \'.css\': \'text/css; charset=utf-8\', \'.json\': \'application/json; charset=utf-8\', \'.svg\': \'image/svg+xml\',\\n  \'.png\': \'image/png\', \'.jpg\': \'image/jpeg\', \'.ico\': \'image/x-icon\' };\\n\\n// The shared records every browser session reads (GET /api/state) and writes (PUT /api/state). A fresh\\n// process starts from the frontend\'s seed.js; `session` and `ui` belong to each browser, never here.\\nfunction loadSeed() {\\n  for (const file of [path.join(DIST, \'seed.js\'), path.resolve(__dirname, \'..\', \'frontend\', \'public\', \'seed.js\')]) {\\n    try {\\n      const sandbox = { window: {} };\\n      vm.runInNewContext(fs.readFileSync(file, \'utf8\'), sandbox, { timeout: 2000 });\\n      const seed = sandbox.window.SEED;\\n      if (seed && typeof seed === \'object\' && !Array.isArray(seed)) {\\n        const shared = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(seed));\\n        delete shared.session; delete shared.ui;\\n        return shared;\\n      }\\n    } catch (e) { console.error(\'seed\', file, e.message); }\\n  }\\n  return null;\\n}\\nlet STATE = loadSeed();\\n\\nfunction json(res, status, body) {\\n  res.writeHead(status, { \'Content-Type\': \'application/json; charset=utf-8\', \'Cache-Control\': \'no-store\' });\\n  res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\\n}\\n\\nfunction readBody(req) {\\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n    const chunks = [];\\n    req.on(\'data\', (c) => { chunks.push(c); if (chunks.reduce((n, b) => n + b.length, 0) > 8e6) req.destroy(); });\\n    req.on(\'end\', () => { try { resolve(chunks.length ? JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString(\'utf8\')) : null); } catch (e) { reject(e); } });\\n    req.on(\'error\', reject);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function api(req, res, url) {\\n  if (url.pathname === \'/api/health\') return json(res, 200, { code: 200, message: \'Backend Ready\' });\\n  if (url.pathname === \'/api/state\') {\\n    if (req.method === \'GET\') return json(res, 200, STATE || {});\\n    if (req.method === \'PUT\') {\\n      const body = await readBody(req);\\n      if (!body || typeof body !== \'object\' || Array.isArray(body)) return json(res, 400, { error: \'state must be an object\' });\\n      STATE = body;\\n      return json(res, 200, { ok: true });\\n    }\\n  }\\n  // Domain routes go here, e.g. if (url.pathname === \'/api/items\' && req.method === \'GET\') ...\\n  return json(res, 404, { error: \'not found\' });\\n}\\n\\nfunction serveStatic(res, pathname) {\\n  let file = path.normalize(path.join(DIST, decodeURIComponent(pathname)));\\n  if (!file.startsWith(DIST)) return json(res, 403, { error: \'forbidden\' });\\n  if (pathname === \'/\' || !fs.existsSync(file) || fs.statSync(file).isDirectory()) file = path.join(DIST, \'index.html\');\\n  const type = TYPES[path.extname(file).toLowerCase()] || \'application/octet-stream\';\\n  res.writeHead(200, { \'Content-Type\': type, \'Cache-Control\': \'no-store\' });\\n  fs.createReadStream(file).on(\'error\', () => { res.end(); }).pipe(res);\\n}\\n\\nconst server = http.createServer(async (req, res) => {\\n  try {\\n    const url = new URL(req.url, \'http://localhost\');\\n    if (url.pathname.startsWith(\'/api/\')) return await api(req, res, url);\\n    return serveStatic(res, url.pathname);\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    console.error(\'handler\', e);\\n    if (!res.headersSent) json(res, 500, { error: \'internal\' }); else res.end();\\n  }\\n});\\nserver.listen(Number(process.env.PORT) || 3000, () => console.log(\'listening\', server.address().port));\\n"}, {"path": "frontend/package.json", "content": "{\\n  \\"name\\": \\"app-frontend\\",\\n  \\"version\\": \\"1.0.0\\",\\n  \\"private\\": true,\\n  \\"scripts\\": { \\"build\\": \\"node -e \\\\\\"require(\'fs\').cpSync(\'public\',\'dist\',{recursive:true})\\\\\\"\\" }\\n}\\n"}, {"path": "frontend/public/app.js", "content": "\'use strict\';\\n// Your application: replace this file. LAYOUT feeds ARC.layout (every screen renders through it);\\n// APP.screen(route) returns the main-content HTML for the current route; APP.actions handle\\n// data-action controls and call ARC.render() after changing ARC.state.\\nwindow.LAYOUT = {\\n  brand: \'App\',\\n  nav: [{ label: \'Home\', hash: \'#/\' }, { label: \'Items\', hash: \'#/items\' }],\\n  sidebar: [{ label: \'Items\', hash: \'#/items\' }],  // optional navigation; specify role only when required\\n  footer: \'\',\\n  account: (user) => user\\n    ? `<span>${ARC.esc(user.name)}</span><button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"logout\\">Sign Out</button>`\\n    : `<a href=\\"#/login\\">Log in</a>`\\n};\\n\\nwindow.APP = {\\n  screens: {\\n    home() {\\n      return `<h1>Home</h1><p>Welcome.</p>`;\\n    },\\n    items() {\\n      const q = (ARC.state.query || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n      // This example uses standalone content cards; choose record semantics from the actual requirements.\\n      const rows = ARC.state.items.filter((it) => !q || it.title.toLowerCase().includes(q)).map((it) => `<article class=\\"row\\">\\n  <h3>${ARC.esc(it.title)}</h3><p>${ARC.esc(it.body)}</p>\\n  ${ARC.rowActions([{ label: \'Edit\', action: \'edit-item\' }, { label: \'Delete\', action: \'delete-item\' }], it.id)}\\n</article>`).join(\'\');\\n      // This example uses a labelled search input; follow any role the requirements specify.\\n      return `<h1>Items</h1><input type=\\"search\\" aria-label=\\"Search\\" data-change=\\"search-items\\"><button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"new-item\\">New Item</button>${rows}`;\\n    },\\n    login() {\\n      return `<h1>Log in</h1><form data-action=\\"login\\">\\n  <label for=\\"email\\">Email</label><input id=\\"email\\" name=\\"email\\" type=\\"email\\">\\n  <label for=\\"password\\">Password</label><input id=\\"password\\" name=\\"password\\" type=\\"password\\">\\n  <button type=\\"submit\\">Log in</button></form>`;\\n    }\\n  },\\n  screen(route) {\\n    const fn = this.screens[route.name] || this.screens.home;\\n    return fn.call(this, route);\\n  },\\n  actions: {\\n    login({ form }) {\\n      const u = ARC.state.users.find((x) => x.email === form.email && x.password === form.password);\\n      if (!u) { ARC.notify(\'Invalid email or password\'); return; }\\n      ARC.state.session = u.id; ARC.save(); ARC.navigate(\'#/\');\\n    },\\n    logout() { ARC.state.session = null; ARC.save(); ARC.navigate(\'#/\'); },\\n    \'new-item\'() {\\n      ARC.openDialog(`<h2>New Item</h2><form data-action=\\"create-item\\">\\n  <label for=\\"title\\">Title</label><input id=\\"title\\" name=\\"title\\">\\n  <button type=\\"submit\\">Save</button> <button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"arc:close\\">Cancel</button></form>`, { title: \'New Item\' });\\n    },\\n    \'create-item\'({ form }) {\\n      ARC.state.items.unshift({ id: ARC.uid(\'i\'), title: form.title, body: \'\' });\\n      ARC.save(); ARC.closeDialog(); ARC.render(); ARC.notify(\'Item created\');\\n    },\\n    \'delete-item\'({ id }) {\\n      const idx = ARC.state.items.findIndex((x) => x.id === id);\\n      const [removed] = ARC.state.items.splice(idx, 1);\\n      ARC.save(); ARC.render();\\n      ARC.notify(\'Item deleted\', { undo: () => { ARC.state.items.splice(idx, 0, removed); ARC.save(); ARC.render(); } });\\n    },\\n    \'edit-item\'({ id }) {\\n      const it = ARC.state.items.find((x) => x.id === id);\\n      ARC.openDialog(`<h2>Edit Item</h2><form data-action=\\"save-item\\" data-id=\\"${ARC.esc(id)}\\">\\n  <label for=\\"title\\">Title</label><input id=\\"title\\" name=\\"title\\" value=\\"${ARC.esc(it.title)}\\">\\n  <button type=\\"submit\\">Save</button> <button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"arc:close\\">Cancel</button></form>`, { title: \'Edit Item\' });\\n    },\\n    \'search-items\'({ el }) { ARC.state.query = el.value; ARC.render(); },\\n    \'save-item\'({ el, form }) {\\n      const it = ARC.state.items.find((x) => x.id === el.dataset.id);\\n      it.title = form.title; ARC.save(); ARC.closeDialog(); ARC.render(); ARC.notify(\'Item saved\');\\n    }\\n  }\\n};\\n"}, {"path": "frontend/public/index.html", "content": "<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\"en\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\"utf-8\\">\\n<meta name=\\"viewport\\" content=\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\">\\n<title>App</title>\\n<link rel=\\"stylesheet\\" href=\\"styles.css\\">\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<!-- Shell. #app is re-rendered synchronously on every state change; the dialog and status roots are\\n     display:none until used so they never intercept pointer events while idle. Script order matters:\\n     seed.js (data) -> lib/arc.js (primitives) -> app.js (your screens, layout config and actions). -->\\n<div id=\\"app\\"></div>\\n<div id=\\"dialog-root\\" hidden></div>\\n<div id=\\"status-root\\" hidden></div>\\n<script src=\\"seed.js\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\"lib/arc.js\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\"app.js\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n"}, {"path": "frontend/public/lib/arc.js", "content": "\'use strict\';\\n// Application primitives. Configure them through LAYOUT and APP, and adapt them to the requirements.\\n(function () {\\n  const ARC = {};\\n\\n  // --- Store: shared records use the server; identity and view state stay in this browser.\\n  // This implementation uses synchronous reads/writes. Seeded collections and arrays are shared;\\n  // session identity uses localStorage, and transient view state uses sessionStorage.\\n  // Choose ownership and lifetime according to the application requirements.\\n  const SEEDED = new Set(Object.keys(window.SEED || {}));\\n  const isShared = (k, v) => k !== \'session\' && k !== \'ui\' && (SEEDED.has(k) || Array.isArray(v));\\n  function split(state) {\\n    const shared = {}, local = {};\\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(state || {})) (isShared(k, v) ? shared : local)[k] = v;\\n    return { shared, local };\\n  }\\n  function sync(method, body) {\\n    try {\\n      const x = new XMLHttpRequest();\\n      x.open(method, \'/api/state\', false);\\n      if (body !== undefined) x.setRequestHeader(\'Content-Type\', \'application/json\');\\n      x.send(body === undefined ? null : body);\\n      return x.status === 200 ? x.responseText : null;\\n    } catch (e) { return null; }\\n  }\\n  function readLocal() {\\n    let local = {};\\n    try { local = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(\'arc:local:v2\') || \'{}\') || {}; } catch (e) {}\\n    try {\\n      const s = localStorage.getItem(\'arc:session:v2\');\\n      if (s !== null) local.session = JSON.parse(s);\\n    } catch (e) {}\\n    return local;\\n  }\\n  ARC.state = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(window.SEED || {}));\\n  // Replace the shared keys with the server\'s copy, in place (code may hold a reference to ARC.state).\\n  ARC.pull = function () {\\n    let data = null;\\n    try { data = JSON.parse(sync(\'GET\') || \'null\'); } catch (e) {}\\n    if (!data || typeof data !== \'object\' || Array.isArray(data) || !Object.keys(data).length) return false;\\n    for (const k of Object.keys(ARC.state)) if (isShared(k, ARC.state[k])) delete ARC.state[k];\\n    Object.assign(ARC.state, split(data).shared);\\n    return true;\\n  };\\n  ARC.save = function () {\\n    const { shared, local } = split(ARC.state);\\n    const { session, ...view } = local;\\n    try { sessionStorage.setItem(\'arc:local:v2\', JSON.stringify(view)); } catch (e) {}\\n    try { localStorage.setItem(\'arc:session:v2\', JSON.stringify(session === undefined ? null : session)); } catch (e) {}\\n    sync(\'PUT\', JSON.stringify(shared));\\n  };\\n  if (!ARC.pull()) sync(\'PUT\', JSON.stringify(split(ARC.state).shared));\\n  Object.assign(ARC.state, readLocal());\\n  ARC.uid = function (prefix) { return (prefix || \'id\') + \'_\' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 9); };\\n  ARC.esc = function (s) { return String(s == null ? \'\' : s).replace(/[&<>\\"\']/g, (c) => ({ \'&\': \'&amp;\', \'<\': \'&lt;\', \'>\': \'&gt;\', \'\\"\': \'&quot;\', \\"\'\\": \'&#39;\' }[c])); };\\n\\n  // --- Router: hash routes, `#/name/param1/param2`.\\n  ARC.route = function () {\\n    const parts = (location.hash || \'#/\').replace(/^#\\\\/?/, \'\').split(\'/\').filter(Boolean).map(decodeURIComponent);\\n    return { name: parts[0] || \'home\', params: parts.slice(1), hash: location.hash || \'#/\' };\\n  };\\n  // Navigation updates the route, shared state and current view together.\\n  ARC.navigate = function (hash) {\\n    if ((location.hash || \'#/\') !== hash) location.hash = hash;\\n    if (ARC.dialogOpen) ARC.closeDialog();\\n    ARC.pull();\\n    ARC.render();\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Shared layout primitives. The application selects the regions its requirements need.\\n  ARC.layout = function (mainHtml, route) {\\n    const L = window.LAYOUT || {};\\n    const user = ARC.currentUser();\\n    const link = (n) => `<a href=\\"${ARC.esc(n.hash)}\\"${route && route.hash === n.hash ? \' aria-current=\\"page\\"\' : \'\'}>${ARC.esc(n.label)}</a>`;\\n    const entry = (n) => n.role === \'button\'\\n      ? `<button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"arc:nav\\" data-hash=\\"${ARC.esc(n.hash)}\\"${route && route.hash === n.hash ? \' aria-current=\\"page\\"\' : \'\'}>${ARC.esc(n.label)}</button>`\\n      : link(n);\\n    const nav = (L.nav || []).map(link).join(\'\');\\n    const side = [...new Set((L.sidebar || []).map(entry))].join(\'\');\\n    const account = L.account ? L.account(user) : \'\';\\n    const brand = !L.brand ? \'\' : L.brandRole === \'button\'\\n      ? `<button type=\\"button\\" class=\\"brand\\" data-action=\\"arc:nav\\" data-hash=\\"#/\\">${ARC.esc(L.brand)}</button>`\\n      : `<a class=\\"brand\\" href=\\"#/\\">${ARC.esc(L.brand)}</a>`;\\n    const header = brand || nav || account ? `<header class=\\"app-header\\">${brand}${nav ? `<nav aria-label=\\"Main navigation\\">${nav}</nav>` : \'\'}${account ? `<div class=\\"account\\">${account}</div>` : \'\'}</header>` : \'\';\\n    return `${header}<div class=\\"layout\\">${side ? `<aside class=\\"sidebar\\">${side}</aside>` : \'\'}<main id=\\"main-content\\" class=\\"main\\">${mainHtml}</main></div>${L.footer ? `<footer class=\\"app-footer\\">${ARC.esc(L.footer)}</footer>` : \'\'}`;\\n  };\\n  ARC.currentUser = function () {\\n    const s = ARC.state;\\n    if (!s || !s.session) return null;\\n    return (s.users || []).find((u) => u.id === s.session) || null;\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Presses: the browser sends `click`, and `dblclick` on a second press, only to an element that is still\\n  // in the document when the button is released. A render inside a mousedown/mouseup handler replaces that\\n  // element and silently drops the click and the double-click (09-24: three of three spreadsheet drafts\\n  // re-rendered their grid on a press, so no cell ever received a click and the double-click editor never\\n  // opened). While a left-button press is in progress, ARC.render() waits for the end of its click sequence\\n  // (after `click`, or after `dblclick` on a second press), in the same task.\\n  let pressing = false, postponed = false;\\n  const settle = () => { pressing = false; if (postponed) { postponed = false; ARC.render(); } };\\n  const press = (ev) => { if (ev.button === 0) pressing = true; };\\n  const release = (ev) => { if (ev.button === 0) { pressing = true; setTimeout(settle, 0); } };\\n  for (const type of [\'pointerdown\', \'mousedown\']) window.addEventListener(type, press, true);\\n  for (const type of [\'pointerup\', \'mouseup\']) window.addEventListener(type, release, true);\\n  window.addEventListener(\'click\', (ev) => { if (ev.detail < 2) settle(); });\\n  // A double-click handler that opened an editor itself (focus is now in a text field of the screen) keeps it:\\n  // the render postponed from the second press would wipe it.\\n  window.addEventListener(\'dblclick\', () => {\\n    const active = document.activeElement, app = document.getElementById(\'app\');\\n    if (active && app && app.contains(active) && active.matches(\'input, textarea, [contenteditable=\\"true\\"]\')) postponed = false;\\n    settle();\\n  });\\n  // A press on a popover belongs to the popover. Grid and list pointer handlers took the cell around a menu as the\\n  // pressed cell and re-selected it, so a menu Copy on a dragged range copied one cell (two of four spreadsheet\\n  // drafts, 09-25). The press still counts above; the click still reaches the popover\'s commands.\\n  for (const type of [\'pointerdown\', \'mousedown\', \'pointerup\', \'mouseup\']) {\\n    window.addEventListener(type, (ev) => {\\n      if (ev.target && ev.target.closest && ev.target.closest(\'[data-popover]\')) ev.stopPropagation();\\n    }, true);\\n  }\\n\\n  // --- Helpers reachable through `this` from any part of APP. A helper written on APP.screens and called as\\n  // `this.helper()` from a screen that runs with APP as `this` (or the other way round, or from an action)\\n  // threw \\"this.helper is not a function\\" and blanked the screen: dozens of drafts on six tasks. Every\\n  // function on APP, APP.screens, APP.actions and APP.helpers is also reachable from the others under the\\n  // same name (non-enumerable, never replacing an own entry); actions run with APP.actions as `this`.\\n  const RESERVED = new Set([\'screen\', \'screens\', \'actions\', \'helpers\', \'afterRender\']);\\n  ARC.shareHelpers = function (app) {\\n    const holders = [app, app && app.screens, app && app.actions, app && app.helpers]\\n      .filter((o) => o && typeof o === \'object\');\\n    for (const from of holders) {\\n      for (const key of Object.keys(from)) {\\n        if (RESERVED.has(key) || typeof from[key] !== \'function\') continue;\\n        for (const to of holders) {\\n          if (to === from || Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(to, key)) continue;\\n          try { Object.defineProperty(to, key, { value: from[key], writable: true, configurable: true, enumerable: false }); } catch (e) { /* frozen */ }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Render: rebuild #app from the store in the same tick as the click. Views are unmounted, never\\n  // cross-faded. Text typed into a form survives in-form clicks because actions call ARC.render()\\n  // only after they change state, and forms keep their values via ARC.preserveInputs.\\n  ARC.render = function () {\\n    if (pressing) { postponed = true; return; }\\n    ARC._ensureSelectStyles();\\n    const route = ARC.route();\\n    ARC._renderedHash = route.hash;\\n    ARC._popover = null;  // the screen is rebuilt; an open popover goes with it\\n    ARC._combobox = null;\\n    const app = window.APP || {};\\n    ARC.shareHelpers(app);\\n    const main = app.screen ? app.screen(route) : \'<h1>Home</h1>\';\\n    document.getElementById(\'app\').innerHTML = ARC.layout(main, route);\\n    if (ARC.dialogOpen) ARC.setInert(true);\\n    if (app.afterRender) app.afterRender(route);\\n    ARC._selectContent(document.getElementById(\'app\'));\\n  };\\n  // --- Dialog: while a chooser is open every sibling is inert + aria-hidden (Playwright ignores\\n  // aria-modal), so no text input outside the dialog is visible to the fill ladder. The root is hidden\\n  // when idle so it never intercepts hovers or clicks.\\n  ARC.dialogOpen = false;\\n  ARC.openDialog = function (html, opts) {\\n    const root = document.getElementById(\'dialog-root\');\\n    root.innerHTML = `<div class=\\"dialog\\" role=\\"dialog\\" aria-label=\\"${ARC.esc((opts && opts.title) || \'Dialog\')}\\">${html}</div>`;\\n    root.hidden = false;\\n    ARC._selectContent(root);\\n    ARC.dialogOpen = true;\\n    ARC.setInert(true);\\n    const first = root.querySelector(\'input, textarea, select, button\');\\n    if (first) first.focus();\\n  };\\n  ARC.closeDialog = function () {\\n    const root = document.getElementById(\'dialog-root\');\\n    root.hidden = true; root.innerHTML = \'\';\\n    ARC.dialogOpen = false;\\n    ARC.setInert(false);\\n  };\\n  ARC.setInert = function (on) {\\n    for (const id of [\'app\', \'status-root\']) {\\n      const el = document.getElementById(id);\\n      if (!el) continue;\\n      if (on) { el.setAttribute(\'inert\', \'\'); el.setAttribute(\'aria-hidden\', \'true\'); }\\n      else { el.removeAttribute(\'inert\'); el.removeAttribute(\'aria-hidden\'); }\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Popover: render contextual UI inside its supplied host. The requirement determines\\n  // the host and whether the interaction is a popover or an entity editor/dialog.\\n  // Command menus are not a replacement for the entity\'s named field editor.\\n  // items are { label, action, extra? }; kind \'buttons\' renders native buttons;\\n  // kind \'menu\' explicitly renders role=menu and role=menuitem.\\n  // The popover closes on render, Escape, a click outside it, and after one of its menu items ran: a menu left\\n  // open inside a grid cell became part of the cell\'s text (\\"PenCopyCutPaste\\" after a menu Cut, 09-25).\\n  // It stays inside the host: apps find the record or cell a command acts on through the menu\'s ancestors.\\n  ARC.openPopover = function (host, items, opts) {\\n    const record = host && host.closest(\'article[data-id], [role=\\"article\\"][data-id]\');\\n    const id = (opts && opts.id) != null ? String(opts.id) :\\n      (host && host.dataset && host.dataset.id) || (record && record.dataset.id) || \'\';\\n    // A menu item may replace its own menu. Keep the connected anchor before removing it.\\n    if (host && ARC._popover && ARC._popover.contains(host)) host = ARC._popover.parentElement;\\n    ARC.closePopover();\\n    if (!host) return;\\n    const kind = (opts && opts.kind) || \'buttons\';\\n    const button = (a) => `<button type=\\"button\\"${kind === \'menu\' ? \' role=\\"menuitem\\"\' : \'\'} data-action=\\"${ARC.esc(a.action)}\\" data-id=\\"${ARC.esc(id)}\\"${a.extra ? \' \' + a.extra : \'\'}>${ARC.esc(a.label)}</button>`;\\n    const body = typeof items === \'string\' ? items : items.map(button).join(\'\');\\n    const wrap = document.createElement(\'div\');\\n    wrap.className = \'popover\';\\n    wrap.setAttribute(\'data-popover\', \'\');\\n    if (kind === \'menu\') { wrap.setAttribute(\'role\', \'menu\'); if (opts && opts.label) wrap.setAttribute(\'aria-label\', opts.label); }\\n    wrap.innerHTML = body;\\n    host.appendChild(wrap);\\n    ARC._selectContent(wrap);\\n    ARC._popover = wrap;\\n  };\\n  ARC.closePopover = function () {\\n    if (ARC._popover && ARC._popover.parentNode) ARC._popover.parentNode.removeChild(ARC._popover);\\n    ARC._popover = null;\\n  };\\n\\n  // Native selects retain form values, keyboard support and standard selection APIs.\\n  // In supporting browsers, the customizable picker also exposes clickable DOM options.\\n  ARC._ensureSelectStyles = function () {\\n    if (!document.head || document.getElementById(\'arc-native-select-style\')) return;\\n    const style = document.createElement(\'style\');\\n    style.id = \'arc-native-select-style\';\\n    style.textContent = \'@supports (appearance: base-select) {\' +\\n      \'select:not([multiple]):not([size]),select:not([multiple]):not([size])::picker(select){appearance:base-select;}\' +\\n      \'select:not([multiple]):not([size]):not(:open) option{display:none;}\' +\\n      \'select:not([multiple]):not([size])::picker(select){background:white;color:#171717;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:6px;padding:4px;}\' +\\n      \'select:not([multiple]):not([size]) option{padding:4px 10px;}\' +\\n      \'select > button.arc-selected-display{all:unset;}\' +\\n      \'}\';\\n    document.head.appendChild(style);\\n    document.addEventListener(\'input\', (event) => {\\n      const el = event.target.closest(\'select.arc-native-combobox[data-cb-change]\');\\n      if (!el) return;\\n      const app = window.APP || {};\\n      const fn = app.actions && app.actions[el.dataset.cbChange];\\n      if (typeof fn !== \'function\') return;\\n      ARC.shareHelpers(app);\\n      fn.call(app.actions, { value: el.value, name: el.name, el, event });\\n    });\\n  };\\n  // Let the browser expose the current value in author DOM while retaining the\\n  // select\'s own value, option nodes, keyboard behavior and change events.\\n  // https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/selectedcontent\\n  ARC._selectContent = function (root) {\\n    if (!window.CSS || !CSS.supports(\'appearance\', \'base-select\') || !window.HTMLSelectedContentElement) return;\\n    ARC._ensureSelectStyles();\\n    for (const select of root.querySelectorAll(\'select:not([multiple]):not([size])\')) {\\n      if (select.querySelector(\':scope > button\')) continue;\\n      const button = document.createElement(\'button\');\\n      button.type = \'button\';\\n      // The select already exposes its value to assistive technology. This\\n      // browser-managed display must not become a second, identically named action.\\n      button.setAttribute(\'aria-hidden\', \'true\');\\n      button.className = \'arc-selected-display\';\\n      button.appendChild(document.createElement(\'selectedcontent\'));\\n      select.prepend(button);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  // ARC.combobox({ label, name, options: [\'A\', \'B\'] | [{value, label}], value, change })\\n  // `change` keeps the existing {value, name, el} callback contract.\\n  ARC.combobox = function (o) {\\n    ARC._ensureSelectStyles();\\n    const id = \'cb-\' + String(o.name || o.label).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, \'_\') + \'-\' + (ARC._cbSeq = (ARC._cbSeq || 0) + 1);\\n    const options = (o.options || []).map((x) => (typeof x === \'object\' ? { value: String(x.value), label: String(x.label != null ? x.label : x.value) } : { value: String(x), label: String(x) }));\\n    const current = options.find((x) => x.value === String(o.value == null ? \'\' : o.value));\\n    return `<span class=\\"combobox\\" data-combobox=\\"${id}\\">` +\\n      `<label id=\\"${id}-label\\" for=\\"${id}\\">${ARC.esc(o.label)}</label> ` +\\n      `<select class=\\"arc-native-combobox\\" id=\\"${id}\\" role=\\"combobox\\" name=\\"${ARC.esc(o.name || \'\')}\\"` +\\n      ` aria-labelledby=\\"${id}-label\\"${o.change ? ` data-cb-change=\\"${ARC.esc(o.change)}\\"` : \'\'}>` +\\n      (current ? \'\' : `<option value=\\"\\" hidden selected>${ARC.esc(o.placeholder || \'Select\')}</option>`) +\\n      options.map((x) => `<option value=\\"${ARC.esc(x.value)}\\"${x === current ? \' selected\' : \'\'}>${ARC.esc(x.label)}</option>`).join(\'\') +\\n      \'</select></span>\';\\n  };\\n  ARC._openCombobox = function (box) {\\n    const wrap = box.closest(\'[data-combobox]\');\\n    const open = wrap.querySelector(\'[role=\\"listbox\\"]\');\\n    ARC.closeCombobox();\\n    if (open) return;  // a second click on an open box closes it\\n    let options = [];\\n    try { options = JSON.parse(box.dataset.options || \'[]\'); } catch (e) {}\\n    const value = (wrap.querySelector(\'input[type=\\"hidden\\"]\') || {}).value;\\n    const list = document.createElement(\'div\');\\n    list.id = box.getAttribute(\'aria-controls\');\\n    list.className = \'listbox\';\\n    list.setAttribute(\'role\', \'listbox\');\\n    list.setAttribute(\'aria-labelledby\', box.getAttribute(\'aria-labelledby\'));\\n    list.innerHTML = options.map((x) => `<div role=\\"option\\" tabindex=\\"-1\\" aria-selected=\\"${x.value === value}\\" data-action=\\"arc:option\\" data-value=\\"${ARC.esc(x.value)}\\">${ARC.esc(x.label)}</div>`).join(\'\');\\n    wrap.appendChild(list);\\n    box.setAttribute(\'aria-expanded\', \'true\');\\n    ARC._combobox = wrap;\\n  };\\n  ARC.closeCombobox = function () {\\n    const wrap = ARC._combobox;\\n    ARC._combobox = null;\\n    if (!wrap) return;\\n    const list = wrap.querySelector(\'[role=\\"listbox\\"]\');\\n    if (list) list.remove();\\n    const box = wrap.querySelector(\'[role=\\"combobox\\"]\');\\n    if (box) box.setAttribute(\'aria-expanded\', \'false\');\\n  };\\n  ARC._pickOption = function (option) {\\n    const wrap = option.closest(\'[data-combobox]\');\\n    const box = wrap.querySelector(\'[role=\\"combobox\\"]\');\\n    const input = wrap.querySelector(\'input[type=\\"hidden\\"]\');\\n    if (input) { input.value = option.dataset.value; input.dispatchEvent(new Event(\'input\', { bubbles: true })); }\\n    box.textContent = option.textContent;\\n    ARC.closeCombobox();\\n    box.focus();\\n    const change = wrap.dataset.cbChange;\\n    const app = window.APP || {};\\n    if (change && app.actions && app.actions[change]) { ARC.shareHelpers(app); app.actions[change]({ value: option.dataset.value, name: input && input.name, el: box }); }\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Clipboard: copy, cut and paste interoperate with the browser and other programs. Text another program\\n  // put there pastes into the app, and what the app copies pastes elsewhere. Outside text fields:\\n  //   ARC.onCopy((cut) => text | { text, data } | null)  Ctrl/Cmd+C or X: the text to put on the clipboard\\n  //     (tab-separated columns, newline-separated rows for a range); `data` is kept for a paste of that same text.\\n  //   ARC.onPaste((text, data) => {})  Ctrl/Cmd+V, and ARC.pasteFromClipboard() for a menu\'s \\"Paste\\" command;\\n  //     `data` is what onCopy kept when the clipboard still holds the text the app copied, else null.\\n  // The native copy/cut/paste events carry the text: never preventDefault a Ctrl+C/X/V keydown, which cancels\\n  // them. When no event follows the keys (a page listener cancelled it), the async clipboard API is used.\\n  let onCopy = null, onPaste = null, copied = null, taken, copySeen = true, pasteSeen = true;\\n  const editing = (el) => !!(el && el.closest && el.closest(\'input, textarea, select, [contenteditable=\\"true\\"], [contenteditable=\\"\\"]\'));\\n  ARC.onCopy = function (fn) { onCopy = fn; };\\n  ARC.onPaste = function (fn) { onPaste = fn; };\\n  const take = (cut) => {\\n    const out = onCopy ? onCopy(cut) : null;\\n    if (out == null) return null;\\n    copied = typeof out === \'object\' ? { text: String(out.text == null ? \'\' : out.text), data: out.data } : { text: String(out), data: null };\\n    return copied.text;\\n  };\\n  // Pasted text arrives with \\\\n line ends and without the one line break that ends copied rows (spreadsheets and\\n  // text editors put it there; it is not an extra empty row).\\n  const lines = (text) => String(text == null ? \'\' : text).replace(/\\\\r\\\\n?/g, \'\\\\n\').replace(/\\\\n$/, \'\');\\n  const give = (text) => {\\n    text = lines(text);\\n    const same = copied && text === lines(copied.text);\\n    if (onPaste) onPaste(text, same ? copied.data : null);\\n  };\\n  // A menu\'s Paste reads the browser clipboard. Where that read is missing, refused (no clipboard permission) or\\n  // does not answer, the app\'s own last copy is pasted instead, so a menu Copy followed by a menu Paste works in\\n  // any browser context.\\n  ARC.pasteFromClipboard = function () {\\n    const own = () => { if (!copied) return false; give(copied.text); return true; };\\n    if (!navigator.clipboard || !navigator.clipboard.readText) return Promise.resolve(own());\\n    return new Promise((resolve) => {\\n      let settled = false;\\n      const finish = (fn) => { if (settled) return; settled = true; clearTimeout(timer); resolve(fn()); };\\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => finish(own), 400);\\n      navigator.clipboard.readText().then(\\n        (text) => finish(() => { if (text === \'\' && copied) return own(); give(text); return true; }),\\n        () => finish(own));\\n    });\\n  };\\n  // A menu\'s \\"Copy\\" / \\"Cut\\" command.\\n  ARC.copyToClipboard = function (cut) {\\n    const text = take(!!cut);\\n    if (text == null || !navigator.clipboard || !navigator.clipboard.writeText) return Promise.resolve(false);\\n    return navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(() => true, () => false);\\n  };\\n  const outside = (ev) => !editing(ev.target) && !editing(document.activeElement);\\n  // The keys read the app\'s selection at once (a later click must not change what is copied); the native event,\\n  // dispatched in the same task, carries the text, and a zero-delay fallback covers a cancelled event.\\n  window.addEventListener(\'keydown\', (ev) => {\\n    const key = (ev.key || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n    if (!(ev.ctrlKey || ev.metaKey) || ev.altKey || key.length !== 1 || !\'cxv\'.includes(key) || !outside(ev)) return;\\n    if (key === \'v\') {\\n      if (!onPaste) return;\\n      pasteSeen = false;\\n      setTimeout(() => { if (!pasteSeen) { pasteSeen = true; ARC.pasteFromClipboard(); } }, 0);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!onCopy) return;\\n    const text = take(key === \'x\');\\n    taken = text;\\n    copySeen = false;\\n    setTimeout(() => {\\n      if (copySeen) return;\\n      copySeen = true; taken = undefined;\\n      if (text != null && navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).catch(() => {});\\n    }, 0);\\n  }, true);\\n  for (const type of [\'copy\', \'cut\']) {\\n    document.addEventListener(type, (ev) => {\\n      if (!onCopy || !outside(ev)) return;\\n      const text = copySeen ? take(type === \'cut\') : taken;\\n      copySeen = true; taken = undefined;\\n      if (text == null || !ev.clipboardData) return;\\n      ev.clipboardData.setData(\'text/plain\', text);\\n      ev.preventDefault();\\n    });\\n  }\\n  document.addEventListener(\'paste\', (ev) => {\\n    if (!onPaste || !outside(ev)) return;\\n    pasteSeen = true;\\n    ev.preventDefault();\\n    give(ev.clipboardData ? ev.clipboardData.getData(\'text/plain\') : \'\');\\n  });\\n\\n  // --- Notification: a role=\\"status\\" element carrying the literal message plus an Undo button.\\n  ARC.notify = function (message, opts) {\\n    const root = document.getElementById(\'status-root\');\\n    ARC._undo = opts && opts.undo;\\n    // Keep the message and any optional action separate.\\n    root.innerHTML = `<div class=\\"status\\" role=\\"status\\"><span class=\\"status-text\\">${ARC.esc(message)}</span>${ARC._undo ? \' <button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"arc:undo\\">Undo</button>\' : \'\'}</div>`;\\n    root.hidden = false;\\n    clearTimeout(ARC._statusTimer);\\n    ARC._statusTimer = setTimeout(() => { root.hidden = true; root.innerHTML = \'\'; ARC._undo = null; }, (opts && opts.ms) || 6000);\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Record actions retain the labels supplied by the application. Styles control their visibility.\\n  ARC.rowActions = function (actions, id) {\\n    return `<div class=\\"row-actions\\">${actions.map((a) => `<button type=\\"button\\" data-action=\\"${ARC.esc(a.action)}\\" data-id=\\"${ARC.esc(id == null ? \'\' : id)}\\"${a.extra ? \' \' + a.extra : \'\'}>${ARC.esc(a.label)}</button>`).join(\'\')}</div>`;\\n  };\\n\\n  // --- Events: one delegated listener. Buttons/links carry data-action; forms carry data-action on the\\n  // <form> and are handled on submit with their fields as an object. APP.actions[name](ctx) receives\\n  // { id, data, el, event, form } and calls ARC.render() itself after changing state.\\n  function dispatch(name, el, event, form) {\\n    const app = window.APP || {};\\n    if (name === \'arc:undo\') { const u = ARC._undo; ARC._undo = null; document.getElementById(\'status-root\').hidden = true; if (u) u(); return; }\\n    if (name === \'arc:close\') { ARC.closeDialog(); return; }\\n    if (name === \'arc:nav\') { ARC.navigate(el.dataset.hash || \'#/\'); return; }\\n    if (name === \'arc:combobox\') { ARC._openCombobox(el); return; }\\n    if (name === \'arc:option\') { ARC._pickOption(el); return; }\\n    const fn = app.actions && app.actions[name];\\n    if (!fn) return;\\n    ARC.shareHelpers(app);\\n    // Act on the records as they are now, including other sessions\' writes. A popover command acts on what the app\\n    // set up when it opened the popover instead: a right-click that selected a cell without saving yet was undone\\n    // by reading the records back, and the command acted on the old selection.\\n    if (!el.closest(\'[data-popover]\')) ARC.pull();\\n    fn.call(app.actions, { id: el.dataset.id, data: { ...el.dataset }, el, event, form });\\n  }\\n  document.addEventListener(\'click\', (ev) => {\\n    if (ARC._popover && !ARC._popover.contains(ev.target) && !ev.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')) ARC.closePopover();\\n    if (ARC._combobox && !ARC._combobox.contains(ev.target)) ARC.closeCombobox();\\n    const el = ev.target.closest(\'[data-action], button, input, textarea, select, a, label\');\\n    if (!el || !el